package com.bqsqwad.heartbreakhealer.feature.entertainment

/** Original ten-part story: The Bridge of Borrowed Bikes. */
internal object StoryLibraryBatch63 {
    val stories = listOf(
        StorySeries(
            id = "the_bridge_of_borrowed_bikes",
            title = "The Bridge of Borrowed Bikes",
            tagline = "A school cycling group works with the council to organise a supervised bicycle library for short community journeys.",
            parts = listOf(
                StoryPart(1, "The Unused Bicycles", listOf(
                    "A community centre had several bicycles donated for a youth activity, but they remained unused because the programme had never developed a maintenance and lending plan. When Kene joined the school's cycling club, he asked whether students could help. The teacher said the bicycles could not be ridden until the centre had checked their condition and insurance arrangements.",
                    "The centre coordinator explained that the bicycles were donations, but ownership records and safety checks still mattered. The club offered to help prepare an inventory. They did not attempt to repair or ride any bicycle; a qualified mechanic would inspect each one."
                )),
                StoryPart(2, "A Proper Inventory", listOf(
                    "The students recorded the visible frame numbers, sizes, and condition notes under staff supervision. The coordinator checked donation records and identified two bicycles whose paperwork needed clarification. Those were set aside until the centre could resolve the records.",
                    "The mechanic inspected the remaining bicycles and found that some needed replacement parts while others were unsuitable for the programme. The students learned that a bicycle could look fine and still require a professional check. The centre arranged the repairs and kept responsibility for approving each bicycle."
                )),
                StoryPart(3, "Who Could Borrow", listOf(
                    "The centre considered how a lending programme might work. It needed clear eligibility, consent arrangements for younger participants, helmet requirements, and a process for checking bicycles in and out. The teacher helped the students list questions but left policy decisions to the centre and its advisers.",
                    "Kene suggested that the programme should focus on supervised community rides rather than unrestricted borrowing. The coordinator agreed that a small pilot would be easier to manage. The centre contacted the council's cycling officer for guidance about safe routes and local requirements."
                )),
                StoryPart(4, "A Route with Support", listOf(
                    "The cycling officer reviewed public routes and identified a short route with designated cycling infrastructure. The group discussed road rules, visibility, and the importance of adult supervision. The students were told that the route could change if conditions or council guidance changed.",
                    "The officer provided official road-safety information for the programme handbook. The club added a reminder that participants must follow current signs and instructions and that no one should ride a bicycle that had not been approved for use. Kene helped turn the information into a simple checklist."
                )),
                StoryPart(5, "The Safety Session", listOf(
                    "Before the pilot, the centre arranged a safety session led by qualified staff. Participants learned how to check basic bicycle fit, wear a correctly fitted helmet, and signal appropriately. The mechanic explained which problems required a bicycle to be taken out of service and assessed by a professional.",
                    "The students practised the checklist with stationary bicycles under supervision. Nobody was encouraged to test an unapproved bicycle on the road. The coordinator recorded attendance and confirmed that the programme's consent and emergency arrangements were in place."
                )),
                StoryPart(6, "The First Ride", listOf(
                    "The centre launched a short supervised ride on the approved route. Staff checked each bicycle before departure, and participants rode at a suitable pace. The group stopped at the planned rest point and returned together. Kene helped distribute the route cards and reminded everyone to follow the ride leader.",
                    "The ride leader collected feedback afterward. Participants liked the route but suggested a clearer sign at the meeting point. One person found the schedule too early, so the centre agreed to review the timing before the next session. The pilot was small by design, allowing staff to make changes safely."
                )),
                StoryPart(7, "A Bicycle Needs Care", listOf(
                    "During the post-ride check, the mechanic noticed that one bicycle needed further attention. It was labelled out of service and stored for repair. The coordinator explained that removing a bicycle from the programme was a normal safety decision, not a punishment or a failure.",
                    "Kene helped update the inventory so the bicycle could not be mistakenly issued. The centre also added a maintenance date to each record. The club learned that a lending programme depended on ongoing checks, not just a successful opening day."
                )),
                StoryPart(8, "The Route Map", listOf(
                    "The cycling officer reviewed the route card and suggested clearer symbols for crossings and rest points. The students redesigned it with a large-print version and a note that riders should always follow current road signs. The council approved the map for the supervised programme.",
                    "The centre displayed the map beside the sign-in desk. It did not publish participants' personal details or exact attendance histories. The coordinator explained how the centre handled records and who could access them. Kene saw that privacy and safety were both part of responsible organisation."
                )),
                StoryPart(9, "More Than a Ride", listOf(
                    "The programme attracted families and young people who wanted to learn about cycling. Some participants joined as riders, while others helped with sign-in, route cards, and refreshments. The centre kept the sessions supervised and limited the number of bicycles to what staff could properly check.",
                    "The council cycling officer visited and praised the careful pilot. They discussed possible future sessions, but the coordinator said expansion would depend on staff capacity, bicycle condition, and funding. The club recorded the feedback and did not promise a larger programme before those checks were complete."
                )),
                StoryPart(10, "A Programme That Moves Carefully", listOf(
                    "At the end of the term, the centre reviewed the pilot. Every bicycle had a current inspection record, the route card had been updated, and participants knew how to register for a supervised session. The two bicycles with unresolved paperwork remained unused until their status could be confirmed.",
                    "Kene wrote a handover guide for next year's cycling club. It explained that donated equipment still needed checks, that routes required current approval, and that a safe programme grew at the pace its people could support. The borrowed bicycles had finally found a purpose, and the bridge they built was one of trust."
                ))
            )
        )
    )
}
